Device Onboarding gives devices that appear for the first time in a DHCP pool
a short, time-limited internet access window (for example 10 minutes),
so that IoT devices can finish their cloud based setup. Afterwards the
regular firewall policy applies again.

Newly seen MAC addresses within the configured address pool are added to
a pf table in the "deviceonboarding" anchor. The entries are removed again
after the configured duration. Known devices never get a second window
unless they are explicitly forgotten.
